# Leave room for effects
@scenario office_lesson_23
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg office]
[char pip global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show pip desk point]
pip: Imagine dust in the beam above the desk. A restrained effect should let the player read the line.
[if !tutorial_still]
[particles dust intensity=0.24 opacity=0.52 speed=0.30 duration=3000]
[endif]
pip: Look between the desks. How much dust can you add before it draws attention away from Pip?
[particles stop]
pip: Change intensity in the particle command and compare the same frame.
@label check
pip: Which comparison tells you whether the effect helps?
> Read the same line with the effect on and off. -> correct
> Check the particle count alone. -> retry
@label retry
[show pip desk curious]
pip: The reader experiences the composed frame, not a counter. Give it another try.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show pip desk cheer]
pip: The reader experiences the composed frame, not a counter.
> Finish this lesson -> return_hub
> Try the lesson again -> start
@label return_hub
[if !tutorial_done_23]
[flag tutorial_done_23]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_5]
